   1137  f6aa							; Line 2: Lives (P0 + P1, green squares) + KEY indicator (the BALL, yellow)
   1138  f6aa							; User 2026-10-27: an EXTRA LIFE every 50,000 points, up to 8, so the row
   1139  f6aa							; draws up to 8 squares: P0 shows min(lives,4), P1 (X 44, flush right of
   1140  f6aa							; P0's 4 squares x 8 px) shows max(lives-4,0). Both are QUAD size (one GRP
   1141  f6aa							; bit = 4 px), squares on bits 7/5/3/1 = 8 px pitch (SquarePat[0..4]).
   1142  f6aa							; The KEY moved from P1 to the BALL (HERO draws its HUD indicators with the
   1143  f6aa							; ball): ENABL=2 only while KeyHeld, COLUPF yellow, 8-clock ball ($35), X 132.
   1144  f6aa							; Budget: 3 SetObjectXPos (P0, P1, ball) + HMOVE + 5 render + 1 gap = 10
   1145  f6aa							; (was 9); the pad line pays for it, see the budget at .HudPad.
