   1441  f875
   1442  f875							; ==============================================================================
   1443  f875							; Raft (enemy type 7) — the moving, rideable platform. plans/raft_moving_plan.md
   1444  f875							; ==============================================================================
   1445  f875							; Entrance: bank0 UEDispatch -> CallPad_RaftBody (sta $1FF5 / jmp $F822) -> here;
   1446  f875							; exit: jmp ReturnPad ($FBF8, bank1's twin) -> bank0's jmp UE_Next.
   1447  f875							; CallPad rules honoured: no nested CallPad, no bank0 jsr, ZP is shared RAM.
   1448  f875							; ZP ALIAS WARNING: this code uses bank0's Temp at $88 (free here — every other
   1449  f875							; overscan Temp consumer, the joystick read and the hot-bump flag, ran before
   1450  f875							; UpdateEnemies). It must NEVER touch bank1's Temp symbol ($AD = bank0's
   1451  f875							; TickCounter — writing that would stall the game timer).
   1452  f875							;
   1453  f875							; User spec 2026-10-18: floats only on water; carries the player across and
   1454  f875							; returns; ~1.5x the player's 1 px/frame; inertia when it starts.
   1455  f875							;   Y	     = the water surface, NOT the authored y and NOT a constant: the
   1456  f875							;	       surface line drifts 0-3 lines with the TIDE (VBL stages 36+off
   1457  f875							;	       into CollisionX, kernel draws the strip as the band's last
   1458  f875							;	       (12-off) lines), so the raft is placed at 125+off and its bottom
   1459  f875							;	       row sits exactly on the moving surface — it rides the wave the
   1460  f875							;	       water does. The rider's pin (top-22 = 103+off, worst case 106)
   1461  f875							;	       stays clear of the 125 water-kill line at every tide phase.
   1462  f875							;	       This write lands after RefreshEnemyY, so the VBL draws it.
   1463  f875							;   Speed   = 1 px on even frames, 2 px on odd (EnemyRamP parity) = 1.5 px/frame.
   1464  f875							;   Inertia = a real spin-up ramp: 1 px/frame for ~30 frames (~0.5 s) then the
   1465  f875							;	       full 1/2 parity (1.5 avg), so the take-off is heavy. The state
   1466  f875							;	       lives in PlayerBombs' ($F0) spare high bits (b7 = ridden flag,
   1467  f875							;	       b6-b3 = level) — the ZP map has no free byte and the bomb count
   1468  f875							;	       keeps b2-0 (see the kernel EQU contract). Stepping off clears the
   1469  f875							;	       flag+level, so the empty raft runs at full speed and the next
   1470  f875							;	       take-off ramps again. It also holds the frame it turns around on.
   1471  f875							;   Range   = derived from the playfield, no data and no ZP: the model row-2
   1472  f875							;	       cell just beyond the raft's leading edge is read from the PF row-2
   1473  f875							;	       buffers and a SOLID cell turns it around, so the raft patrols
   1474  f875							;	       exactly the open water span of the room.
   1475  f875							;   Ride    = the raft is a FERRY: it moves ONLY while the player's box overlaps
   1476  f875							;	       its upper rows; step off and it parks immediately (the ramp state
   1477  f875							;	       is cleared too, so the next take-off ramps again). While over it a
   1478  f875							;	       non-rising player (vyHi >= 0) is pinned to the raft's top with vy
   1479  f875							;	       zeroed (gravity must never accumulate into the water) and carried
   1480  f875							;	       by the raft's step; thrust up skips the pin but keeps the carry, so
   1481  f875							;	       flying off is always possible. Leaving and re-entering the ROOM
   1482  f875							;	       resets the raft to its authored spawn x (LoadEnemyRam re-copies
   1483  f875							;	       it), which is the "reset" the user asked for.
   1484  f875							; In: X = enemy slot. Clobbers A/Y and bank0 Temp ($88).
   1485  f875							; ==============================================================================
   1486  f875							; RaftCellSolid — is the model row-2 (water row) playfield cell in display
   1487  f875							; column A solid? Reflect mapping: CTRLPF $35 (reflect) is the cave default and
   1488  f875							; a raft room has no door/bar band to switch it off. IN: A = display col 0..39.
   1489  f875							; OUT: Z=1 open (water) / Z=0 solid. Clobbers A/Y.
   1490  f875							;   cols 0-3	-> PF0 row 3 ($C6), bit 4+col (PF0 bit 4 = leftmost pixel)
   1491  f875							;   cols 4-11	-> PF1 row 3 ($CA), bit 7-(col-4)
   1492  f875							;   cols 12-19 -> PF2 row 3 ($CE), bit col-12
   1493  f875							; (row 3 = the bottom/water band of a 4-band room. These read $C5/$C8/$CB, the
   1494  f875							; rows of the old 3-band stride-3 layout, until 2026-10-28: the raft then turned
   1495  f875							; at ceiling/ledge cells that were not on its water row.)
   1496  f875							;   cols 20-39 -> the mirrored half: source = 39-col
   1497  f875				   RaftCellSolid
   1498  f875		       c9 14		      cmp	#20
   1499  f877		       90 05		      bcc	.RCSrc
   1500  f879		       49 ff		      eor	#$ff
   1501  f87b		       18		      clc
   1502  f87c		       69 28		      adc	#40
   1503  f87e				   .RCSrc
   1504  f87e		       a8		      tay
   1505  f87f		       b9 97 f8 	      lda	RaftCellMasks,Y
   1506  f882		       c0 04		      cpy	#4
   1507  f884		       b0 03		      bcs	.RCPF1
   1508  f886		       25 c6		      and	$C6	; PF0Buf+3: the water row (4 bands; was +2 = band 3)
   1509  f888		       60		      rts
   1510  f889				   .RCPF1
   1511  f889		       c0 0c		      cpy	#12
   1512  f88b		       b0 03		      bcs	.RCPF2
   1513  f88d		       25 ca		      and	$CA	; PF1Buf+3 (stride 4; $C8 was row 1)
   1514  f88f		       60		      rts
   1515  f890				   .RCPF2
   1516  f890		       25 ce		      and	$CE	; PF2Buf+3 (stride 4; $CB was row 0)
   1517  f892		       60		      rts
