   1838  fabb							; (PairGone RETIRED, plan 5.1b 2026-10-20: the cell punch guards a repeat
   1839  fabb							;  blast on the PF buffer itself — the punched cell pair is empty, so a
   1840  fabb							;  second blast in the same room cannot score again. No rect idx4, no mask.)
   1841  fabb
   1842  fabb							; ========================================================================
   1843  fabb							; BombMarkWalls (S5.2, moved from bank0) — pinned at $FB10.
   1844  fabb							;   On the bomb 1->2 edge: punch the THIN walls in the blast window and
   1845  fabb							;   report how many were newly broken (A, caller scores +75 each).
   1846  fabb							;   Bomb left-half col +-2, clamped 0..19. Score is NOT done here — pads
   1847  fabb							;   cannot nest (ReturnPad switches to bank0), so the bank0 caller adds
   1848  fabb							;   +75 per wall.
   1849  fabb							;   Plan 5.1b (2026-10-20): the punch is CELL-based — no rect cache. The
   1850  fabb							;   PF buffers ARE the map (export: convert_room.pf_values; holes included),
   1851  fabb							;   so a bombable wall is found the same way find_rectangles finds a w==2
   1852  fabb							;   rect: a thin wall is ONE D7 logical cell = 2 display cols = a solid
   1853  fabb							;   PF bit-PAIR whose left and right neighbouring cells are empty. The
   1854  fabb							;   emitted cells are pair-aligned (both bits of a cell are always written
   1855  fabb							;   together: pf_values, ClearPFColumn, PhMaskTab), so ONE solidity read
   1856  fabb							;   per cell covers both cols, and vertical extent needs no data: each row
   1857  fabb							;   is tested on its own (the old rect h is exactly the run of thin rows —
   1858  fabb							;   find_rectangles stops a w==1 rect at a row that joins a wider run, and
   1859  fabb							;   so does the neighbour test). Col 0 (screen border, and its mirror col
   1860  fabb							;   39) is never destroyable — the old `rect.x == 0` skip.
   1861  fabb							;   Double-score guard = the buffer: the punched pair is empty, so a second
   1862  fabb							;   blast in the same room finds no cell (the old WallMask bits and PairGone
   1863  fabb							;   are gone; walls return on re-entry, D1-B). WallMask (BombPacked b3-6) is
   1864  fabb							;   retired: HotOverlapBody now tests its parent hot cell's PF bit.
   1865  fabb							;   Cost: ≤4 cells × 3 rows × ~3 cell probes; blast edge only.
   1866  fabb							; ========================================================================
   1867  fabb							; AddScoreCarry — the rare path of AddScore (>= 100 points carried out of ScoreTe).
   1868  fabb							; Entered with D=1 and C=1. Ripples the carry through ScoreHu and ScoreTh; a
   1869  fabb							; carry INTO ScoreTh is a 10,000-point crossing, and ScoreTh's low digit
   1870  fabb							; (ten-thousands) is then 0 or 5 exactly on a 50,000 / 100,000 mark — that is
   1871  fabb							; the EXTRA LIFE (user 2026-10-27: every 50,000, max MAX_LIVES = 8). A carry out
   1872  fabb							; of ScoreTh means 999,999 + more: the score sticks at 999,999. Runs once per
   1873  fabb							; 100 points at most, and each 10,000 crossing happens once, so no life can be
   1874  fabb							; awarded twice for the same mark. Tested by tools/test_addscore.py.
   1875  fabb				   AddScoreCarry
   1876  fabb		       a5 f4		      lda	ScoreHu
   1877  fabd		       69 00		      adc	#0	; + the carry (BCD)
   1878  fabf		       85 f4		      sta	ScoreHu
   1879  fac1		       90 18		      bcc	.ASCdone	; no 10,000 crossing
   1880  fac3		       a5 f3		      lda	ScoreTh
   1881  fac5		       69 00		      adc	#0	; + the carry (BCD)
   1882  fac7		       b0 16		      bcs	.ASCcap	; past 999,999
   1883  fac9		       85 f3		      sta	ScoreTh
   1884  facb		       29 0f		      and	#$0F	; ten-thousands digit
   1885  facd		       f0 04		      beq	.ASClife	; x0,000 : 100,000 / 200,000 ...
   1886  facf		       c9 05		      cmp	#5
   1887  fad1		       d0 08		      bne	.ASCdone	; only x5,000... i.e. 50,000 / 150,000 ...
   1888  fad3				   .ASClife
   1889  fad3		       a5 ac		      lda	PlayerLives
   1890  fad5		       c9 08		      cmp	#MAX_LIVES
   1891  fad7		       b0 02		      bcs	.ASCdone
   1892  fad9		       e6 ac		      inc	PlayerLives
   1893  fadb				   .ASCdone
   1894  fadb		       d8		      cld
   1895  fadc		       4c f8 fb 	      jmp	ReturnPad
   1896  fadf				   .ASCcap
   1897  fadf		       a9 99		      lda	#$99
